# 1️⃣ LINKED LIST — THE BIG IDEA

Unlike an array, linked-list elements are connected using pointers.

```text
HEAD
 ↓
[10 | •] → [20 | •] → [30 | NULL]
```

Each node contains:

```text
Data + Next Pointer
```

### Python Representation

```python
class ListNode:
    def __init__(self, val=0, next=None):
        self.val = val
        self.next = next
```

---

# 2️⃣ ARRAY vs LINKED LIST 🧠

| Array                                            | Linked List                                  |
| ------------------------------------------------ | -------------------------------------------- |
| Contiguous memory concept                        | Nodes connected by references                |
| Fast index access                                | Sequential access                            |
| O(1) indexing                                    | O(n) indexing                                |
| Insertion can require shifting                   | Easier insertion once position/node is known |
| Fixed/dynamic implementation depends on language | Naturally dynamic structure                  |

### Interview Line:

> **Arrays provide fast random access, while linked lists provide flexible node-based insertion and deletion.**

